Jay Boghawala jvb73


Design notes:
- malloc(0) returns a 16 byte chunk instead of NULL
- free(NULL) does nothing
- requests bigger than the heap are rejected before rounding, so huge sizes like SIZE_MAX cant overflow
- if splitting would leave less than 16 bytes the caller gets the whole chunk, so the leak count can include a few padding bytes
- free merges right away, so two free chunks are never next to each other and malloc never has to merge
- freeing a pointer again after its chunk merged into a neighbor is still caught, since that chunks header is gone
- after a bad free, exit(2) still runs the leak detector, so a leak message can show up after the error
- MEMLENGTH defaults to 4096 but can be changed at compile time with -DMEMLENGTH=N (N should be a multiple of 8)
- tests and memgrind hardcode for 4096 byte heap since they cant see MEMLENGTH


Building:
make               builds memgrind and tests
make clean         removes the executables

Test programs:
./tests            normal tests, prints PASS/FAIL for each
./tests notmalloc  free(&x)
./tests middle     free(p+1)
./tests twice      free the same pointer twice
./tests leak       leaks 2 objects on purpose

The bad free ones should print an error and exit 2 (check with echo $?)
They run one at a time since exit(2) ends the program


./memgrind         runs 5 tasks 50 times, prints the average time per run
1. malloc 8 to 1024 bytes, free in reverse order
2. malloc 120 1-byte objects, free in the same order
3. randomly malloc 1 byte or free one until 120 mallocs, then free the rest
4. fill the heap, free every other one, refill the holes with random sizes, check nothing got overwritten, free all
5. fill the heap with 256 1-byte objects, free in random order, then malloc the whole heap


Test plan:
1. malloc doesn't overlap objects
   detect: objects keep the bytes we wrote
   test: fill the heap with 64 objects, each its own byte, check them (./tests)

2. free gives memory back
   detect: freed memory can be malloced again
   test: malloc the whole heap, free it, malloc it again (./tests)

3. free chunks next to each other merge
   detect: a request bigger than any single freed chunk still fits
   test: fill the heap with 24 byte chunks, free all, malloc 48 (./tests)
   test: fill the heap with 1 byte objects, free in random order, malloc the whole heap (memgrind task 5)
   test: fill the heap with 3 chunks, free the outer two then the middle, malloc the whole heap (./tests)

4. malloc reports when it can't allocate
   detect: returns NULL, prints "malloc: Unable to allocate ..."
   test: malloc(4097) (./tests)

5. free on something not from malloc
   detect: prints "free: Inappropriate pointer ...", exits 2
   test: free(&x) (./tests notmalloc)

6. free in the middle of a chunk
   detect: same error, exits 2
   test: free(p+1) (./tests middle)

7. double free
   detect: same error, exits 2
   test: free the same pointer twice (./tests twice)

8. leaks get reported
   detect: prints "mymalloc: N bytes leaked in M objects." at exit, nothing if no leaks
   test: malloc 20 twice without freeing, should say 48 bytes in 2 objects (./tests leak)

